{% block cms_block_three_linked_category_image_panels %}
    {# A dedicated grid with zero gap keeps all three cards touching; no Bootstrap column gutters between cards. #}
    {#
        OPTIONAL ALTERNATIVE: normal image above the text, instead of a background image.
        This is documentation only; everything inside this Twig comment is disabled.

        Keep the loop and zero-gap grid below. To use this alternative, replace the
        sw_include inside "if element" with the markup below, or put the markup in
        a separate CMS element template for reuse. The existing resolver already
        supplies category.media and the category URL, so no resolver change is needed.

        Use a separate card class: cms-element-image-panel applies background-image
        styling and an overlay, which this normal image layout does not need.

        {% set category = element.data.category %}
        {% set config = element.translated.config|default(element.config) %}
        {% if category and element.data.url %}
            <a class="linked-category-image-card" href="{{ element.data.url }}"
               {% if category.shouldOpenInNewTab %}target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"{% endif %}>
                {% if category.media %}
                    {% sw_thumbnails 'linked-category-card-image' with {
                        media: category.media,
                        sizes: { lg: '33vw', default: '100vw' },
                        attributes: {
                            class: 'linked-category-image-card__image',
                            alt: category.media.translated.alt|default(category.translated.name),
                            loading: 'lazy'
                        }
                    } %}
                {% endif %}
                <div class="linked-category-image-card__content">
                    <h3>{{ category.translated.name }}</h3>
                    {% if config.text.value|default('') %}<p>{{ config.text.value }}</p>{% endif %}
                </div>
            </a>
        {% endif %}

        sw_thumbnails renders a normal <img> with responsive srcset attributes.
        The whole image and text remain one link; there is no button.
        Add these styles to the storefront SCSS only when enabling this alternative:

        .linked-category-image-card {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            width: 100%;
            min-width: 0;
            color: inherit;
            text-decoration: none;
        }
        .linked-category-image-card__image {
            display: block;
            width: 100%;
            height: auto;
            aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
            object-fit: cover;
        }
        .linked-category-image-card__content { padding: 24px; }
        .linked-category-image-card:focus-visible {
            outline: 3px solid currentColor;
            outline-offset: -3px;
        }

        No margin or gap is added between cards; padding is inside the text area.

        ADMINISTRATION CHANGES FOR THE NORMAL-IMAGE VERSION
        Paths below are relative to:
        src/Resources/app/administration/src/module/sw-cms/

        1. elements/linked-category-image-panel/component/
           In sw-cms-el-linked-category-image-panel.html.twig, replace the
           background style binding with a normal image above the H3 and paragraph:

           <img v-if="category && category.media"
                :src="category.media.url"
                :alt="category.media.translated?.alt || categoryName"
                class="linked-category-image-card__image">

           Keep the category loader and categoryName computed property in index.js.
           Remove the cardStyle binding/computed property if it is no longer used.
           In sw-cms-el-linked-category-image-panel.scss, remove the background
           and overlay styling and style the image and text as separate areas.
           Use display: block; width: 100%; height: auto on the image.
           The admin canvas should preview the card without a clickable category
           link, so clicking it still opens the CMS editing controls.

        2. elements/linked-category-image-panel/preview/index.js
           Update the element picker preview to show an image placeholder above
           the category heading, rather than a heading over a background.

        3. blocks/text-image/three-linked-category-image-panels/preview/
           Update sw-cms-preview-three-linked-category-image-panels.html.twig
           and its SCSS to show three normal-image cards. Keep gap: 0.

        The element config/ and registration index.js remain the same: the editor
        still selects a category and an optional paragraph, with no image picker.
        The block registration, three named slots and component grid also stay
        the same. The PHP resolver already supplies the category media and URL.

        After changing administration templates or styles, run from the project root:
        docker compose exec -T web bash bin/build-administration.sh

        Compile the theme for storefront SCSS changes and clear the cache for
        storefront Twig changes when you actually enable this alternative.
    #}
    <div class="col-12">
        <div class="three-image-panels-grid">
            {% for index in 1..3 %}
                {% set element = block.slots.getSlot('card-' ~ index) %}
                <div class="three-image-panels-column"{% if element %} data-cms-element-id="{{ element.id }}"{% endif %}>
                    {% if element %}
                        {% sw_include '@Storefront/storefront/element/cms-element-' ~ element.type ~ '.html.twig' with { element: element } %}
                    {% endif %}
                </div>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
